#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1333 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: AEDUR present but AEENDTC ABSENT altogether. This is the worst case the sheet describes - resolved, no end date collected at all, no duration - yet the machine-emitted var_exists(AEENDTC) conjunct makes the leaf false and the rule reports NOTHING; AEENDTC is not in Requirements.Variables so the silence is not an auditable skip. Pins CURRENT behaviour (finding SD1333-F1). RESOLVED 2026-09-11 (T1-30): the ruling put AEENDTC in Requirements.Variables.Any [AEENDTC, AEDUR], NOT All -- the sheet asks for an end date OR a collected duration, so either column suffices -- and the present AEDUR column satisfies the gate here: the verdict stays violation, pinning the OTHER Any entry than invalid_no_aedur does. Only a dataset with neither column skips, and the sister PMDA-SD9724 reports it. FRESH - no twin equivalent; deliberate contrast to invalid_no_aedur."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEOUT   type=Char label="Outcome of Adverse Event"
col AEDUR   type=Char label="Duration of Adverse Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | NAUSEA | RECOVERED/RESOLVED |
